  const [unit, setUnit] = useState('celsius');

  const handleConvert = (toUnit) => {
    switch (toUnit) {
      case 'fahrenheit':
        setTemperature((temperature * 9 / 5) + 32);
        break;
      case 'kelvin':
        setTemperature(temperature + 273.15);
        break;
      default:
        break;
    }
    setUnit(toUnit);
  };

  return { temperature, unit, handleConvert };
};

export default useTemperatureConverter;
```

This hook provides a `temperature` state, an `unit` state, and a `handleConvert` function that can be used to convert temperatures between Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin. The `handleConvert` function takes a `toUnit` parameter that specifies the desired output unit, and it updates the `temperature` and `unit` states accordingly.

To use this hook in a component, you can import it and call the `useTemperatureConverter` function:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useTemperatureConverter } from './use-temperature-converter';

const TemperatureConverter = () => {
  const { temperature, unit, handleConvert } = useTemperatureConverter();

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Temperature Converter</h2>
      <p>Current temperature: {temperature} {unit}</p>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('fahrenheit')}>Convert to Fahrenheit</button>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('kelvin')}>Convert to Kelvin</button>
    </div>
  );
};

export default TemperatureConverter;
```

This component displays the current temperature in the selected unit and provides buttons to convert it to Fahrenheit or Kel

