To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. **Create an Auth0 account**: If you don't have one already, sign up for an Auth0 account at <https://auth0.com/>.

2. **Set up a new Auth0 application**: After logging in, click on the "Applications" tab and then click on "Create Application." Choose "Web Apps" as the application type and fill out the required information.

3. **Configure the Auth0 application**: In the "Settings" tab of your newly created application, find the "Allowed Callback URLs" section. Add the callback URL for each of your React apps here, separated by a comma. This will allow Auth0 to redirect users back to the correct app after authentication.

4. **Enable SSO**: In the same "Settings" tab, scroll down to the "SSO" section. Enable the "SSO" option and choose the SSO protocol you want to use (e.g., SAML, OIDC). Follow the instructions provided by Auth0 to configure the SSO settings for your application.

5. **Integrate Auth0 into your React apps**: Now that you have set up Auth0 for your applications, you need to integrate it into your React apps. You can do this using the `@auth0/auth0-react` library. First, install the library using npm or yarn:

