To leverage the Accord.NET library in C# to train and implement the Naive Bayes algorithm for text classification, follow these steps:

1. Install the Accord.NET NuGet package.
2. Load your dataset of labeled sentences into a list of strings, where each string represents a sentence with its corresponding category (sports, politics, or entertainment).
3. Create a NaiveBayes classifier object and fit it on the dataset.
4. Use the CountVectorizer class to transform the dataset into a matrix of word counts.
5. Predict the labels of new observations using the fitted model.
6. Demonstrate the classification process using a sample sentence and output the predicted label.

Here's a concise and elegant C# code that accomplishes this task:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Bayes;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Transformations;

namespace TextClassification
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            // Load your dataset of labeled sentences into a list of strings
            var dataset = new List<string>
            {
                "Sports game was exciting",
                "Politician made a controversial statement",
                "Entertainer gave an amazing performance"
            };

            // Create a NaiveBayes classifier object and fit it on the dataset
            var classifier = new NaiveBayes();
            classifier.Fit(dataset);

            // Use the CountVectorizer class to transform the dataset into a matrix of word counts
            var vectorizer = new CountVectorizer();
            var transformedDataset = vectorizer.Transform(dataset);

            // Predict the labels of new observations using the fitted model
            var newSentence = "The sports game was exciting";
            var prediction = classifier.Predict(newSentence);

            // Demonstrate the classification process using a sample sentence and output the predicted label
            Console.WriteLine($"Sample sentence: {newSentence}");
            Console.WriteLine($"Predicted label: {prediction}");
        }
    }
}
```

