export default class ManageRegistrationScreen extends React.Component {
 state = {
 registrations:[]
 }
}

checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {

 console.log("mnpphoneno: " + mnpPhoneNo);

 var headers = new Headers();
 headers.append("Authorization", "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken());
 fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), mnpPhoneNo), {
 headers: headers,
 method: 'GET'
 })
 .then(r => r.json())
 .then(rjson => {
 this.state.registrations[b].mnpStatus = rjson.status;
 })
 }

I have an array as above. This array is set inside the registrations state. The checkMNPStatusAPI is a function
that I call so that it can push another parameter of variable, such as "portInStatus: 1" in each of the data inside
the registrations state. How can I achieve this if I want to push the variable into the registrations state?

response:
To push the `mnpStatus` value from the API response into the corresponding object in your `registrations` state array, you can use the `map` function and update the state using `setState`. Here's an example:

```javascript
checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
  // ... (rest of the code remains the same)

  const updatedRegistrations = this.state.registrations.map((registration, b) => {
    if (b === index) {
      return { ...registration, mnpStatus: rjson.status };
    }
    return registration;
  });

  this.setState({ registrations: updatedRegistrations });
}
```

This will update the `mnpStatus` property in the specified object within the `registrations` state array with the value received from the API response.

Here's a PowerShell script that recursively checks folders for ACLs referring to SIDs in the SIDHistory of users or groups in the domain:

```powershell
# Define the folder path to start with
$folderPath = "C:\YourFolderPath"

# Function to check if an ACL refers to a SID in the SIDHistory
function CheckACL($acl) {
    $sidHistory = @()

    # Iterate through each access control entry (ACE) in the ACL
    foreach ($ace in $acl) {
        # Check if the ACE refers to a SID in the SIDHistory
        if ($ace.IdentityReference -match '^S-1-5-21-(\d+)-(\d+)-(\d+)-(\d+)$') {
            $sidHistory += $ace.IdentityReference
        }
    }

    # Return true if any SIDs in the SIDHistory are present in the domain
    return ($sidHistory | ForEach-Object { Get-ADUser -Filter { SamAccountName -eq $_ } }) -ne $null
}

# Recursively check folders for ACLs referring to SIDs in the SIDHistory
function CheckFolders($folderPath) {
    Get-ChildItem -Path $folderPath -Directory | ForEach-Object {
        $acl = Get-Acl -Path $_.FullName
        if (CheckACL($acl)) {
            Write-Host "Folder: $($_.FullName)"
            CheckFolders($_.FullName)
        }
    }
}

# Start checking folders
CheckFolders($folderPath)
```

Replace `C:\YourFolderPath` with the folder path you want to start with. This script will recursively check all subfolders for ACLs referring to SIDs in the SIDHistory and print out the folder paths if any are found.
